## User Review Required

We want to highlight three major structural connection systems for your review:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **1. Production-Safe CORS Middleware on FastAPI**
> We will configure the FastAPI CORS middleware in `main.py` using dynamic environment-based origins instead of insecure wildcards (`"*"`):
> - Reading a comma-separated list of origins (e.g. `http://localhost:3000,https://your-frontend.vercel.app`) from `.env`.
> - Allowing `credentials=True` (crucial for cookies and auth headers), `allow_methods=["*"]`, and `allow_headers=["*"]`.
> - Properly resolving preflight `OPTIONS` requests.

> [!TIP]
> **2. Robust Reconnecting WebSockets with Heartbeats**
> To prevent WebSockets from silently dropping due to proxy timeouts (e.g. Render/Railway idling connections after 30-60s of inactivity), our `websocket.ts` service will:
> - Send a periodic heartbeat (ping/pong) every 20 seconds.
> - Automatically attempt reconnection with exponential backoff if disconnected.
> - Dispatch events to trigger graceful UI fallback states and browser toasts if the backend goes offline.

> [!WARNING]
> **3. Firebase Admin Token Verification & Mock Fallback**
> In `backend/app/core/security.py`, we will implement the Firebase Admin SDK token decoder (`firebase_admin.auth.verify_id_token`).
> To ensure the backend is **fully operational and testable immediately out of the box** even before you copy your Firebase Service Account JSON credentials, we will build an intelligent local testing fallback: if the credentials JSON is missing or `ENVIRONMENT="development"`, the verification engine will decode the token or fallback to a secure developer claim (`dev-operator-admin`), printing a warning in the console!

